Package: lagTables
Title: Lag Sequential Analysis Tables and Plots
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Joseph", "Bonito", email = "jbonito@email.arizona.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Computes lag sequential statistics for categorical event
    sequence data -- transition probability tables, log-linear models of
    lag order/stationarity, and standardized-residual plots -- and
    renders the results as html tables, following the log-linear
    approach to lag sequential analysis described in Poole, M. S. (2000)
    in Poole & Van de Ven, "Organizational Change and Innovation
    Processes."
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
Imports: dplyr,
          tidyr,
          tibble,
          DescTools,
          ggplot2,
          rlang,
          knitr,
          kableExtra,
          broom,
          purrr,
          magrittr
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
